@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Read recorded closure outcomes
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "SprintHistoryPage / SprintHistoryView" as page
  participant "ISprintService / SprintService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "SprintsController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "GetSprintHistoryQueryHandler\nGetSprintOutcomesQueryHandler\nGetSprintScopeChangesQueryHandler" as handler
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Open a closed sprint from the Sprints tab history list
page -> page : SprintHistoryPage reads the workspace (IWorkspaceService.workspaceResource) for the breadcrumb\nand the project name; a workspace 404 shows Project not found with Back to projects (project-not-found)
page -> client : Three caller-owned resources: header, outcomes page 1, scope changes page 1 (page size 25)
client -> access : GET .../sprints/{sprintId}/history, .../history/outcomes, .../history/scope-changes
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once; sign in with this history route as return route
else Authenticated (profile P: every active role reads sprints)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send the typed query through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-045 page 1 or more; page size 1-100, default 25
  alt Invalid page or page size
    validation --> ctrl : 400 field errors; nothing read
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : That section shows the page-size message without Try again or reference ID\n(the view always sends page size 25, so only direct API callers meet this)
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle the query
    handler -> db : L2-026 LoadSprintHistoryHeaderAsync (snapshot header with the initial scope count),\nor ListSprintOutcomesAsync (recorded order, then story ID) / ListSprintScopeChangesAsync (newest first by\natUtc, then story ID): one page with its total in one statement
    db --> handler : Recorded rows and totals, or no snapshot
    alt Workspace missing (the page's workspace read also answers 404)
      handler --> ctrl : 404
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : Project not found with Back to projects, decided by the page's workspace read
    else Sprint missing or in another workspace; or a header or outcome read of a sprint not closed
      handler --> ctrl : 404
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : Sprint not found state with Back to sprints, naming the project
    else Snapshot found
      opt Outcome page (batched lookup, never per row)
        handler -> db : One batched lookup: which of this page's recorded story IDs still exist, and their current titles
        db --> handler : Live IDs and titles (links and renamed notes only)
      end
      handler --> ctrl : Header with full completed, carried-over and returned counts;\nor a page of recorded rows with its total
      ctrl --> client : 200
      client --> page : Each resource updates its own value signal; deleted stories show recorded ID, title,\nstatus and a Deleted label without a link; scope changes show recorded text only
      page --> actor : Present recorded fields, start and close actors, scope changes, outcomes, and any pager
    end
  end
end
opt Try again after a failed read
  actor -> page : Choose Try again
  page -> page : SprintHistoryView emits retryRequested; the page reloads its workspace resource and increments\nits counter, so the view's refresh input rereads all three resources together
end
loop Change page in outcomes or scope changes
  actor -> page : Choose a page in one list
  page -> client : That list's page signal changes; its resource aborts a superseded read
  client --> page : New page of that list only; the header and the other list are unchanged
end
note over ctrl, db
History stays readable in Kanban mode. No snapshot edit endpoint exists;
closed-sprint mutations return 409 (L2-026.3).
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043);
the page shows Load failed with the reference ID and Try again; a read
that gets no response shows the same state without a reference ID.
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
